---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import { getTeam } from '../../lib/content';

const team = await getTeam();
const collider = await getEntry('notes', 'collider-spotlight');
if (!collider?.data.url) throw new Error('About page needs the collider-spotlight note with a url.');
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Data for Humans is a small team that helps mission-driven organizations make sense of their data and of what their people know. Rochester and the Twin Cities, working nationally."
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Minnesota roots · Working nationally" title="A small team you work with directly." accent>
    <p class="lede">
      Data for Humans is a small team that helps mission-driven organizations make sense of their data and of what their
      people know. Chris Roberts founded the firm in 2021 to grow data capacity in the nonprofit and public sectors.
    </p>
    <p>
      We work from Rochester and the Twin Cities, remotely by default and on site when a project needs it. You work
      directly with the people doing the work.
    </p>
  </PageHeader>

  <Section rail="Team" labelledby="h-team">
    <h2 id="h-team" class="visually-hidden">Team</h2>
    <ul class="team" role="list">
      {
        team.map((p) => (
          <li class="person" id={p.id}>
            {p.data.photo && p.data.photoAlt && (
              <Image class="person__photo" src={p.data.photo} alt={p.data.photoAlt} width={240} height={240} />
            )}
            <div class="person__text">
              <h3 class="person__name">
                {p.data.name}
                {p.data.credentials && <>, {p.data.credentials}</>}
              </h3>
              <p class="person__role mono">{p.data.role}</p>
              <p>{p.data.bio}</p>
              {p.data.linkedin && (
                <p>
                  <a href={p.data.linkedin}>
                    LinkedIn<span class="visually-hidden">: {p.data.name}</span>
                  </a>
                </p>
              )}
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section rail="Roots" labelledby="h-roots">
    <h2 id="h-roots">Where we come from</h2>
    <!-- Current site text, rewritten without dashes (spec). -->
    <p>
      Our roots run through both ends of Minnesota: the Twin Cities, where Michael spent two decades building public data
      systems at Hennepin and Ramsey Counties, and Rochester, where Chris has built dashboards and reporting
      infrastructure for county initiatives and regional nonprofits. That's where we learned this work, and it's still
      where a good share of it happens.
    </p>
    <p>
      But the problems don't stop at a state line. A coalition trying to see itself in one picture, a program officer
      asking for evidence you can't easily produce, a client tracked in three systems that don't talk: we've seen the same
      knots everywhere we've worked. What matters most is knowing how funders, public agencies and multi-agency
      initiatives actually operate, and what a small team can realistically maintain after we're gone.
    </p>
    <p>
      So we work wherever the need is. Engagements run remotely by default, with on-site time when a project genuinely
      calls for it, and we'll tell you plainly when it does.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section rail="Method" labelledby="h-how">
    <h2 id="h-how">How we work</h2>
    <ol class="ledger" role="list">
      <li class="ledger__row">
        <p class="ledger__num mono">01</p>
        <div class="ledger__body">
          <h3>Plain language, always</h3>
          <p>No jargon and no black boxes. If your team can't understand and use what we build, we haven't finished the job.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="ledger__row">
        <p class="ledger__num mono">02</p>
        <div class="ledger__body">
          <h3>Your tools, your way</h3>
          <p>We work with the systems you already run and the way your team already operates.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="ledger__row">
        <p class="ledger__num mono">03</p>
        <div class="ledger__body">
          <h3>Tailored to reality</h3>
          <p>We size the work to your actual budget and capacity.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="ledger__row">
        <p class="ledger__num mono">04</p>
        <div class="ledger__body">
          <h3>Listen first</h3>
          <p>
            Every project starts with conversations with the people who do the work, because they know things the data
            doesn't.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </Section>

  <Section rail="Press" labelledby="h-news">
    <h2 id="h-news">In the news</h2>
    <p>
      Collider: <a href={collider.data.url}
        >“Putting Data to Work for Good: How Chris Roberts Is Helping Nonprofits Make a Bigger Impact,”</a
      > Nov 9, 2026. <a href={`/notes/${collider.id}/`}>Our note</a>.
    </p>
  </Section>
</Base>
